  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Supporting School Reconstruction within Mozambique Disaster Risk Management and Resilience Program</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The ultimate goal of the project is the resilient//retrofitting of 3,000 classrooms spread across the country&apos;s coastal provinces, including those that have recently been affected by cyclones Idai and Keneth. The technical approach for the rehabilitation of the 3,000 classrooms will aim to integrate improved technical measures through work with construction units of school infrastructures at provincial level (UCEE) and its staff, improving the capacities of the contractors, supervisors, government technicians and in the awarding contracts for rehabilitation/retrofitting of conventional classrooms.</narrative>
  </description>
